### Playtest: a seeded 3-player game through two battles.
# Start the server with `mise run server`, then run the requests top to bottom in IntelliJ.
# Seed 42 deals: anna 4 Horde + Wood + Essence, ben 4 Horde + 2 Essence, cleo 4 Horde + Iron + Wood.
# Counters: Bow beats Mage, Sword beats Bow, Mage beats Sword (+1 attack in that duel).
@host = http://localhost:8080

### Create a game for 3 players; anna hosts
POST {{host}}/games
Content-Type: application/json

{ "players": 3, "host": "anna", "seed": 42 }

> {% client.global.set("gameId", response.body.gameId); %}

### ben joins
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "ben" }

### cleo joins — the game is full and turn 1 starts
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "cleo" }

### anna's view: BUILD_UP, pot 1, her hand, available actions
GET {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}?player=anna

### ── Turn 1: build-up ──────────────────────────────────────────────

### anna upgrades a Horde into a Bow (Horde + Wood)
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/anna/upgrades
Content-Type: application/json

{ "into": "BOW" }

### ben upgrades a Horde into a Mage (Horde + Essence)
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/ben/upgrades
Content-Type: application/json

{ "into": "MAGE" }

### ben upgrades a second Horde into a Mage
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/ben/upgrades
Content-Type: application/json

{ "into": "MAGE" }

### cleo upgrades a Horde into a Sword (Horde + Iron)
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/cleo/upgrades
Content-Type: application/json

{ "into": "SWORD" }

### anna is ready
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/anna/ready

### ben is ready
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/ben/ready

### cleo is ready — the battle starts
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/cleo/ready

### ── Turn 1: battle (everyone keeps their upgrades hidden) ──────────
# Duels: anna–ben 2:2, anna–cleo 2:0, ben–cleo 2:0 → scores anna +2, ben +2, cleo −4.
# anna and ben tie at the top, so nobody wins and the victory point rolls over.

### anna commits 2 Horde and keeps her Bow back
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/anna/army
Content-Type: application/json

{ "HORDE": 2 }

### ben commits 2 Horde and keeps his Mages back
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/ben/army
Content-Type: application/json

{ "HORDE": 2 }

### cleo sits this one out — the battle resolves
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/cleo/army
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### ben's view: battle 1 in the log with no winner; turn 2 with a pot of 2
GET {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}?player=ben

### ── Turn 2: build-up (no upgrades) ──────────────────────────────

### anna is ready
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/anna/ready

### ben is ready
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/ben/ready

### cleo is ready — the battle starts
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/cleo/ready

### ── Turn 2: battle (three armies of 2, decided by a counter) ──────
# Duels: anna–ben 3:2 (anna's Bow counters ben's Mages), anna–cleo 2:2, ben–cleo 2:2
# → scores anna +1, ben −1, cleo 0. Equal sizes, so anna wins the double pot through her Bow.

### anna commits her Bow and 1 Horde
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/anna/army
Content-Type: application/json

{ "BOW": 1, "HORDE": 1 }

### ben commits his 2 Mages (they would counter a Sword, but nobody brings one)
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/ben/army
Content-Type: application/json

{ "MAGE": 2 }

### cleo commits 2 Horde and keeps her Sword back — the battle resolves
POST {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}/players/cleo/army
Content-Type: application/json

{ "HORDE": 2 }

### anna's view: battle 2 won by anna with the double pot (2 VP); turn 3 with a pot of 1
GET {{host}}/games/{{gameId}}?player=anna
